WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.780
How would you know that a vesicle carries a message?

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.720
Start with how vesicles are collected.

3
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.080
Slow spins remove cells and debris.

4
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.520
A faster spin removes large vesicles.

5
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:23.320
About 100,000 times gravity, for an hour or more, brings down the small ones.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:29.303
The pellet holds everything of the right size and density, whatever it is.

7
00:00:29.803 --> 00:00:36.003
That includes protein aggregates, lipoprotein particles, viruses, and vesicles from

8
00:00:36.003 --> 00:00:37.363
the calf serum in the medium.

9
00:00:38.543 --> 00:00:41.123
Soluble growth factors can stick to any of these.

10
00:00:41.863 --> 00:00:44.343
These contaminants have changed conclusions.

11
00:00:45.303 --> 00:00:49.983
In 2019, Robert Coffey's laboratory separated such pellets further.

12
00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:55.823
Argonaute proteins, which carry microRNA, were not detected in the exosomes.

13
00:00:56.617 --> 00:00:59.737
So a claim needs controls.

14
00:01:00.797 --> 00:01:06.017
Purify further, most often by floating the pellet on a sucrose density gradient.

15
00:01:06.977 --> 00:01:12.957
Membrane vesicles rise to about 1.13 to 1.19 grams per millilitre.

16
00:01:13.577 --> 00:01:15.257
Free protein stays below.

17
00:01:16.277 --> 00:01:18.857
Ask whether the activity moves with the vesicles.

18
00:01:18.857 --> 00:01:25.677
Test the supernatant left after the spin, and a pellet from medium that never saw cells.

19
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:32.790
And count. Copies per vesicle is cargo copies measured, divided by particles

20
00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:39.130
counted. If that number is far below one, or if the effect needs many more vesicles

21
00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:44.230
than the donor cells release, the case for signalling is weak, however clean the

22
00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.850
pellet. Your turn.

23
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:52.210
Spin the medium from cell type A, add the pellet to cell type B, and B changes.

24
00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.330
Which controls do you need?

